return array(
	'about_h' => 'About',
	'about_lede' => 'Kikan College is a plumbing and heating apprenticeship college at 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield, founded in 2009 by Rosa Lindqvist and Emeka Obi in a former foundry workshop. The two bench halls are on the ground floor and are step-free.',
	'about_rail' => 'ABOUT · 2009',
	'about_rule1' => 'Not a quick certificate',
	'about_rule2' => 'Not online: the bench is the course',
	'about_rule3' => 'No gas work on live homes in Year 1',
	'about_s1_h' => 'The foundry workshop',
	'about_s1_p1' => 'In 2009 Rosa Lindqvist, a master plumber, and Emeka Obi, a heating engineer, rented the old foundry workshop and set six benches in it. That workshop is still the college. Rosa is principal and leads Bench Hall A. Emeka is head of heating and leads Bench Hall B and the boiler rig. The address is 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield. The office phone is +00 44 555 0193 and the email is hello@kikan-college.example.',
	'about_s1_p2' => 'There is one course: two years, intake every September, 24 places in two groups of 12. Year 1 is spent at the bench in these halls. Year 2 is spent with a working firm. Eighteen placement partners sit within 40 km of Wrenfield. The line we keep for the college is the same one on the door: warm homes start at the bench.',
	'about_s2_h' => 'Why adults',
	'about_s2_p1' => 'The course is for adults who want a trade they can see working. Career changers come from other jobs and start with no trade experience, which is allowed. People returning to work after time away sit in the same groups. School leavers over 18 who want a bench, not a lecture hall, are welcome too. The minimum age is 18 and there is no upper age. Monday to Thursday are bench days.',
	'about_s2_p2' => 'Friday is theory: water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings, and safe working. The work is repetitive in a useful way. Pipe is cut, bent, and joined until the sequence sits in the hands. A day is meant to end with something that either holds or can be named and redone. That is the room we built, and it is why the college takes adults of any age over 18.',
	'about_s3_h' => 'What we are not',
	'about_s3_p1' => 'Kikan College is not a quick certificate, and the course is not online. There is no gas work on live homes in Year 1. In Year 2, gas or electrical work happens only under the placement firm\'s qualified engineer. We do not name an accreditation body or a public qualification. What the college signs is the bench assessments and the signed logbook.',
	'about_s3_p2' => 'We do not publish employment rates. A placement is a training year, not a job offer. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it. The course is two years: 38 teaching weeks from September to July in the bench year, then the placement year on the same calendar, with 24 places each September.',
	'about_s4_h' => 'Two halls',
	'about_s4_p1' => 'Bench Hall A is Rosa Lindqvist\'s hall. Apprentices learn pipework, soldering, bending, and drainage there. Hana Petrović teaches soldering and pipework in that hall. Bench Hall B is Emeka Obi\'s hall, with the boiler rig, controls, and heat pumps. Luis Carvalho teaches heat pumps and controls, and he takes the Friday theory day. Both halls are on the ground floor of the old foundry workshop, and both are step-free.',
	'about_s4_p2' => 'At the end of a teaching day the bays are swept by 15:30. At dusk the task lamps can still be lit over the practice rigs, with the tall factory windows gone blue. Visitors on a Tuesday at 16:00 see these rooms after the bench day has finished.',
	'about_s5_h' => 'A college day',
	'about_s5_p1' => 'The college office is open Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30. Bench halls run Monday to Thursday from 07:45 to 15:30, and on Friday from 08:30 to 15:30. A Monday-to-Thursday day starts with tool check and toolbox talk at 07:45 and ends at 15:30 when the logbook is signed and the bay is swept. Friday theory runs 08:30–12:30, lunch is 12:30–13:15, and open bench and resits run 13:15–15:30.',
	'about_s5_p2' => 'Taster Saturday is the first Saturday of every month, 09:00–15:00, and it does not run in August. The evening refresher is on Tuesdays, 18:00–21:00, for people already in the trade. Those hours are the same ones printed with the fees and on the contact page.',
	'about_s6_h' => 'Next steps',
	'about_s6_p1' => 'Come to a taster Saturday, or visit on a Tuesday at 16:00. Applications for September close on 30 April. Apply online or by email at hello@kikan-college.example. The next meeting is a bench morning and a talk, 90 minutes, in which you cut and join one piece of pipe. Nobody expects that piece to be good. An offer letter follows within 10 working days.',
	'about_s6_p2' => 'A EUR 300 deposit holds the place and counts towards Year 1. Year 1 is EUR 4,800 and Year 2 is EUR 2,400. Year fees can be paid in ten monthly instalments at no extra cost. The office answers the phone on +00 44 555 0193 during Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30.',
