	'apply_s1_h' => 'Come to a taster Saturday or a Tuesday visit',
	'apply_s1_p1' => 'Come to a taster Saturday or a Tuesday visit at 16:00. Taster Saturday is the first Saturday of every month, 09:00–15:00, and it does not run in August. The morning needs no booking. Boots and glasses are provided, and lunch is included. The day is free. A Tuesday visit at 16:00 is the shorter look, after the bench day has finished, in the same halls.',
	'apply_s1_p2' => 'The address is 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield. Both bench halls are on the ground floor and are step-free. The office is open Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30, on +00 44 555 0193, if you want to ask which Saturday is next before you travel.',
	'apply_s2_h' => 'Apply online or by email',
	'apply_s2_p1' => 'Apply online or by email. Applications for September close on 30 April. For the September 2027 intake, that date is 30 April 2027. Write to hello@kikan-college.example. Tell us your name, what you do now, and which September you want to start. We reply within five working days with a date for a bench morning. You need to be 18 or over.',
	'apply_s2_p2' => 'There is no upper age, and no previous trade experience is needed. The intake is 24 places, two groups of 12. The form asks which September, 2027 or 2028, whether you have been to a taster Saturday, and for your consent that Kikan College may contact you about this application.',
	'apply_s3_h' => 'A bench morning and a talk',
	'apply_s3_p1' => 'A bench morning and a talk lasts 90 minutes. You cut and join one piece of pipe. Nobody expects it to be good. The point is to stand at a bay in Bench Hall A or Bench Hall B, under a task lamp, and see whether a day of this kind of work is the day you want. Instructors stay with you for that piece.',
	'apply_s3_p2' => 'It is not an exam, and it is not scored as one of the bench assessments. It is the conversation the offer is based on, together with what you have already told us about the work you do now. Wear clothes you can work in. If you do not yet have boots or glasses, say so when the date is set.',
	'apply_s4_h' => 'An offer letter',
	'apply_s4_p1' => 'An offer letter comes within 10 working days. A EUR 300 deposit holds the place and counts towards Year 1. Year 1, the bench year, is EUR 4,800 for 38 weeks, four bench days and one theory day, September to July. Year 2, the placement year, is EUR 2,400 for four days placed, one college day, and three site visits.',
	'apply_s4_p2' => 'The starter tool kit is EUR 640 in week 1, yours to keep. The workwear and safety pack is EUR 180 in that same week. Year fees can be paid in ten monthly instalments at no extra cost. Placement firms pay apprentices a training wage in Year 2; the amount is agreed with each firm.',
	'apply_s5_h' => 'Who can apply',
	'apply_s5_p1' => 'The course is for adults. The minimum age is 18 and there is no upper age. No previous trade experience is needed. Career changers, people returning to work, and school leavers over 18 who want a bench rather than a lecture hall all sit in the same groups of 12. The course is not online, and it is not a quick certificate.',
	'apply_s5_p2' => 'There is one intake each September, 24 places. You apply for a named September, and the application closes on 30 April of that year. If you are already in the trade and want only the evening refresher, that is a separate line: six Tuesday evenings, 18:00–21:00, at EUR 390. It does not use one of the 24 places.',
	'apply_s6_h' => 'Office hours',
	'apply_s6_p1' => 'The college office is open Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30. The phone is +00 44 555 0193 and the email is hello@kikan-college.example. The address is 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield. If the form is not available, email your application to that address. Tell us your name, what you do now, and which September you want to start.',
	'apply_s6_p2' => 'We reply within five working days with a date for a bench morning. Bench halls run Monday to Thursday 07:45–15:30 and Friday 08:30–15:30, so a visit at 16:00 on a Tuesday finds the teaching day finished and the halls still open to look at. Both halls are step-free, on the ground floor.',
