	'course_h' => 'The course',
	'course_lede' => 'The course at Kikan College is two years, with one intake every September and 24 places in two groups of 12. Year 1 is at the bench in Wrenfield; Year 2 is four days a week with a partner firm and Fridays back at college.',
	'course_rail' => 'THE COURSE · TWO YEARS',
	'course_s1_h' => 'Year 1 — the bench year',
	'course_s1_p1' => 'Year 1 runs for 38 teaching weeks, from September to July. Four days, Monday to Thursday, are bench days in the halls at 22 Foundry Lane. Bench Hall A covers pipework, soldering, bending, and drainage. Bench Hall B covers the boiler rig, controls, and heat pumps. Friday is the theory day: water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings, and safe working. The bench day starts at 07:45 and ends at 15:30.',
	'course_s1_p2' => 'There is no gas work on live homes in this year. Pressure tests and fault-finding stay on the practice boiler rig. The fee for the bench year is EUR 4,800. In week 1 you receive the starter tool kit and the workwear and safety pack. No previous trade experience is needed, and the course is not online.',
	'course_s2_h' => 'Year 2 — the placement year',
	'course_s2_p1' => 'Year 2 runs from September to July. You spend four days a week placed with a partner firm and one day at college on Friday. Grace Mwangi, the placement coordinator, visits every Year 2 apprentice on site, once each term. The fee covers those three site visits and is EUR 2,400. The firm pays a training wage; the amount is agreed with each firm.',
	'course_s2_p2' => 'Gas or electrical work in this year happens only under the firm\'s qualified engineer. A placement is a training year, not a job offer. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it. Eighteen firms within 40 km of Wrenfield take part. The college day on Friday keeps the logbook tied to the year out on site.',
	'course_s3_h' => 'Inside the two years',
	'course_s3_p1' => 'Six strands run through the two years. Pipework is the daily handling of pipe on the bench, measured and cut to the drawing. Soldering and bending cover the joints and the hand bender, the work Hana Petrović stays close to in Bench Hall A. Drainage sits with the rest of that hall. The boiler rig is the afternoon work in Emeka Obi\'s hall: pressure tests and fault-finding.',
	'course_s3_p2' => 'Heat pumps and controls are Luis Carvalho\'s subject, on the rig and on Friday. The theory day is Friday, 08:30–12:30, on water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings, and safe working, then open bench and resits from 13:15 to 15:30 after lunch. None of these strands is offered as a short certificate, and none of them is taught online.',
	'course_s4_h' => 'Assessment and the logbook',
	'course_s4_p1' => 'Each year includes the bench assessments and the signed logbook, at EUR 220 per year. We do not attach the name of an outside award or a public qualification to that record. The logbook is written and signed at the end of a bench day, between 15:00 and 15:30, after the bay is swept. Friday afternoons, 13:15–15:30, are when resits sit on the open bench. An instructor can keep an apprentice back on those Fridays when a joint is not yet reliable.',
	'course_s4_p2' => 'Hana Petrović did that for a whole first term when soldering was slow. The point of the record is simple: someone can see what you have done with your hands, week by week, and sign it. That signed logbook is what you carry between the bench year and the placement year.',
	'course_s5_h' => 'The year in months',
	'course_s5_p1' => 'Year 1 is marked at three points: a September start, a mid-year review in February, and the bench assessment in July. Year 2 is marked at three points as well: the placement starts in September, a site visit falls in each term, and the final assessment is in June. Between those marks the week does not change its shape. In Year 1, Monday to Thursday stay on the bench and Friday stays in the theory room for 38 teaching weeks.',
	'course_s5_p2' => 'In Year 2 the four placement days belong to the firm and Friday belongs to the college. Intake is every September, with 24 places, two groups of 12. Applications for that September close on 30 April. The minimum age is 18 and there is no upper age.',
	'course_s6_h' => 'Next steps',
	'course_s6_p1' => 'A useful first visit is Taster Saturday, the first Saturday of the month from 09:00 to 15:00, except August, or a Tuesday visit at 16:00. The bench morning that follows an application lasts 90 minutes. You cut and join one piece of pipe, and nobody expects it to be good. An offer letter comes within 10 working days.',
	'course_s6_p2' => 'A EUR 300 deposit holds an offered place and counts towards the Year 1 fee of EUR 4,800. Year fees can be paid in ten monthly instalments at no extra cost. Write to hello@kikan-college.example or call +00 44 555 0193. The office is open Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30, at 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield.',
