	'day_c1_h' => 'Morning at the bench',
	'day_c1_p' => 'Between a quarter to eight and half past twelve you cut, bend and joint. The first block is the week’s measuring and cutting; after a short break the second block turns it into the week’s piece, an assembly of copper pipe that has to hold pressure on Friday. Instructors walk the benches and check joints with a torch, not a lecture.',
	'day_c2_h' => 'Afternoon on the rig',
	'day_c2_p' => 'After lunch the group moves to the boiler rig. You pressure-test the pipework you made, bleed a radiator circuit and learn to read a gauge and a fault. The rig is made a little wrong each week on purpose, because finding the fault is the lesson and the repair is the easy part.',
	'day_c3_h' => 'End of the day',
	'day_c3_p' => 'The last half hour belongs to the logbook. You write down what you made and what went wrong, your instructor signs it, and the bay is swept before anyone goes home. The signed logbook is what the bench assessments are marked from, so it matters more than it looks.',
