	'ins_founders_h' => 'The two founders',
	'ins_h' => 'Instructors',
	'ins_link' => 'Meet the instructors →',
	'ins_n' => '05',
	'ins_role3' => 'Instructor, soldering and pipework',
	'ins_role4' => 'Instructor, heat pumps and controls',
	'ins_role5' => 'Placement coordinator',
	'ins_sub' => 'Five people, named, who teach every day.',
	'ins_team_h' => 'Instructors and the placement coordinator',
	'ins_where3' => 'Bench Hall A',
	'ins_where4' => 'Bench Hall B and the Friday theory room',
	'ins_where5' => 'Year 2 site visits',
	'instructors_h' => 'Instructors',
	'instructors_lede' => 'Five people teach and place the course: Rosa Lindqvist, Emeka Obi, Hana Petrović, Luis Carvalho, and Grace Mwangi. They share two bench halls and the Friday theory day at 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield.',
	'instructors_rail' => 'INSTRUCTORS · FIVE',
	'instructors_s1_p1' => 'Rosa Lindqvist is principal and co-founder, a master plumber, and she leads Bench Hall A. She and Emeka Obi rented the foundry workshop in 2009 and set six benches in it. Hall A is where pipework, soldering, bending, and drainage are taught on the Monday-to-Thursday bench days. Her standard in the hall is the standard the bench assessments sit against: a joint that holds, a run that follows the drawing, a bay left swept at 15:30.',
	'instructors_s1_p2' => 'She still treats the college as a workshop that keeps an office, open Monday to Friday from 08:00 to 16:30. The course she leads is two years, in person, for adults of 18 and over, with no upper age and no trade experience required. Questions for the principal go through hello@kikan-college.example or +00 44 555 0193.',
	'instructors_s2_p1' => 'Emeka Obi is co-founder and head of heating. He leads Bench Hall B and the boiler rig. The afternoon block, 13:15–15:00, is the rig block: pressure testing and fault-finding on that rig. He teaches apprentices to watch the work until they can say whether it is holding, and then to write that down in the logbook before 15:30. He does not send Year 1 onto live gas in people\'s houses.',
	'instructors_s2_p2' => 'Any gas or electrical work waits for Year 2, and then only under the placement firm\'s qualified engineer. The boiler rig, the controls, and the heat pumps live in his hall. Luis Carvalho teaches the heat-pump and controls side and the Friday theory day. The two of them share Bench Hall B without turning the bench year into site work.',
	'instructors_s3_h' => 'Hana Petrović',
	'instructors_s3_p1' => 'Hana Petrović is an instructor for soldering and pipework, in Bench Hall A with Rosa Lindqvist\'s groups. She will keep someone back on a Friday afternoon if the joint is not ready. Friday open bench and resits run 13:15–15:30. She says it plainly: nobody is good at soldering in week one. By June you will not remember why it was hard. That line is the shape of her term.',
	'instructors_s3_p2' => 'The first bench block, 08:00–10:15, and the second, 10:35–12:30, are where most of her teaching sits, on cutting, bending, and jointing, after the 07:45 tool check and around the 20-minute break. Farid Haddad\'s first term was slow at soldering, and it was Hana who kept him back on Fridays until the work caught up. The logbook is signed only when that work is fit to sign.',
	'instructors_s4_h' => 'Luis Carvalho',
	'instructors_s4_p1' => 'Luis Carvalho is an instructor for heat pumps and controls, and he teaches the Friday theory day. Friday theory runs from 08:30 to 12:30 and covers water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings, and safe working. After lunch, 13:15–15:30 is open bench and resits, when the morning subjects meet the practical work again. Heat pumps are also a placement path: two of the 18 partner firms are heat-pump installers.',
	'instructors_s4_p2' => 'Ingrid Solberg was placed with a heat-pump installer and now plans the pipe runs on site. Luis\'s teaching stays inside the college week. Year 1 has no gas work on live homes, so his Friday is not a site visit. Grace Mwangi is the person who visits Year 2 apprentices on site. Luis\'s room is the theory room, then the open bench.',
	'instructors_s5_h' => 'Grace Mwangi',
	'instructors_s5_p1' => 'Grace Mwangi is the placement coordinator. She does not run a bench hall. She matches Year 2 apprentices to the 18 partner firms within 40 km of Wrenfield, and she visits every one of them on site, once each term. A firm commits to four days a week, one named engineer, and those three visits. Her sentence to applicants is the college\'s sentence. A placement is a training year, not a job offer.',
	'instructors_s5_p2' => 'Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it. The Year 2 fee of EUR 2,400 includes the Friday at college and the three site visits. The training wage is agreed with each firm, and Grace does not publish a figure for it. Employers who want to take an apprentice ask for her through the office on +00 44 555 0193.',
	'instructors_s6_h' => 'Who teaches which day',
	'instructors_s6_p1' => 'Monday to Thursday, 07:45–15:30, Bench Hall A is led by Rosa Lindqvist, with Hana Petrović on soldering and pipework. Bench Hall B is led by Emeka Obi, and the boiler rig fills the afternoon block from 13:15 to 15:00. Luis Carvalho teaches heat pumps and controls and takes Friday, 08:30–12:30, in the theory room, then the open bench until 15:30.',
	'instructors_s6_p2' => 'Grace Mwangi is with Year 2 apprentices on site for one visit each term, while their other Friday hours are the college day. The evening refresher on Tuesdays, 18:00–21:00, is six evenings for people already in the trade, at EUR 390, and it sits outside the apprenticeship week. Five people, two halls, one theory day, one coordinator on the road.',
	'instructors_strip' => 'FIVE PEOPLE',
	'lang_label' => 'Language',
	'list_h' => 'News',
	'list_n' => '01',
	'list_p' => 'Bench notes and placement stories from the college.',
	'newsletter_h' => 'College letter',
	'newsletter_lede' => 'The college letter is a monthly note from Kikan College: the next taster dates, one bench tip, and one placement note. You are not on the list until the office replies.',
	'newsletter_rail' => 'COLLEGE LETTER · MONTHLY',
	'newsletter_s1_h' => 'What the letter holds',
	'newsletter_s1_p1' => 'Each month the letter carries three things and no more. First, the taster dates: the next first Saturday, 09:00–15:00, and a reminder that August has none. Second, one bench tip from the halls, the sort of thing Hana Petrović or Emeka Obi would say at a bay, short enough to use on a Monday. Third, one placement note from Grace Mwangi, about the year with a firm, written so it stays inside the rule: a placement is a training year, not a job offer.',
	'newsletter_s1_p2' => 'The letter does not publish fees as a new list, employment rates, or the name of any award. Fees stay on the fees page, in euros, and they do not change inside the letter.',
	'newsletter_s2_h' => 'How to ask for it',
	'newsletter_s2_p1' => 'Leave your email and send the request to hello@kikan-college.example. The message subject is the college letter. Sending the message asks for the letter. You are not on the list until we reply. The office replies within five working days, in office hours, Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30. If you would rather write in your own words, use the same address and say you want the monthly letter.',
	'newsletter_s2_p2' => 'The phone is +00 44 555 0193. The letter is free. It is not an application. Applications for September still close on 30 April, and a place is held only by the EUR 300 deposit after an offer letter.',
	'newsletter_s3_h' => 'What it will not do',
	'newsletter_s3_p1' => 'The letter will not tell you that a firm will keep you on. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it. It will not quote an employment rate, because we do not publish one. It will not rename the bench assessments and the signed logbook as something else. It will not announce a new course.',
	'newsletter_s3_p2' => 'There is one course, two years, intake every September, 24 places. If a fee changes it will be changed on the fees page first, in the same seven lines: Year 1 EUR 4,800, Year 2 EUR 2,400, the kit EUR 640, workwear EUR 180, assessment EUR 220 per year, the evening refresher EUR 390, and Taster Saturday free.',
	'newsletter_strip' => 'LETTER',
