	'pc3_l' => 'visits from the college, one each term',
	'pc3_n' => '3',
	'pl1_l' => 'Small heating firms',
	'pl1_n' => '7',
	'pl1_t' => 'Family-run firms of two to ten people: boiler services, repairs and new systems.',
	'pl2_l' => 'Housing maintenance teams',
	'pl2_n' => '5',
	'pl2_t' => 'Planned repairs and heating upgrades across social and rented homes.',
	'pl3_l' => 'Commercial plumbing contractors',
	'pl3_n' => '4',
	'pl3_t' => 'Larger buildings: plant rooms, hot water and drainage.',
	'pl4_l' => 'Heat-pump installers',
	'pl4_n' => '2',
	'pl4_t' => 'Low-carbon heating: pipe runs, controls and commissioning.',
	'pl_b1' => 'Placements for apprentices →',
	'pl_b2' => 'Take an apprentice →',
	'pl_h' => 'Where graduates are placed',
	'pl_n' => '04',
	'pl_note' => 'A placement is a training year, not a job offer. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it.',
	'pl_p' => 'Grace Mwangi, our placement coordinator, matches each apprentice to a firm in the spring of Year 1. She looks at where you live, what you enjoyed at the bench and which engineer is likely to be a good teacher, and she visits every Year 2 apprentice on site once a term. If a placement is not working, she moves you, and the college stays your base.',
	'pl_sub' => 'Eighteen firms within 40 km of Wrenfield.',
	'pl_total' => '18 partner firms within 40 km of Wrenfield',
	'placements_h' => 'Placements',
	'placements_lede' => 'Year 2 places each apprentice with one of 18 partner firms within 40 km of Wrenfield, four days a week, with Fridays back at college. Grace Mwangi matches people to firms and visits every apprentice on site once a term.',
	'placements_rail' => 'YEAR 2 · PLACEMENTS',
	'placements_s1_h' => 'How matching works',
	'placements_s1_p1' => 'Grace Mwangi is the placement coordinator. She visits every Year 2 apprentice on site, once each term, three visits across the year. Matching is done against the kind of work a firm actually does and the way someone has worked on the bench in Year 1. The bench assessments and the signed logbook are the record she can walk through with a firm. She does not sell a job at the end of it.',
	'placements_s1_p2' => 'A placement is a training year, not a job offer. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it. The Year 2 fee is EUR 2,400, from September to July, and it covers four days placed, the Friday at college, and the three site visits. The placement starts in September, with a site visit in each term and a final assessment in June.',
	'placements_s2_h' => 'Eighteen firms, four kinds',
	'placements_s2_p1' => 'The 18 partners divide into four kinds, and the counts are the whole ledger. Seven are small heating firms. Five are housing maintenance teams. Four are commercial plumbing contractors. Two are heat-pump installers. All of them sit within 40 km of Wrenfield. The stories on this site name the kinds of site three apprentices actually had: a four-person heating firm in Wrenfield, a housing maintenance team, and a heat-pump installer.',
	'placements_s2_p2' => 'Those are three people\'s placements, not a menu you can order from. Firms differ in size and in the work of the week. The college\'s rule does not differ: the placement year is training, four days with the firm and Friday at 22 Foundry Lane.',
	'placements_s3_h' => 'Site visits and the training wage',
	'placements_s3_p1' => 'The apprentice is with the firm four days a week. One day, Friday, is at the college. Grace Mwangi\'s visit is one site visit each term. She sees the work and speaks with the named engineer, and the year stays tied to the logbook. Gas or electrical work is done only under the firm\'s qualified engineer. Placement firms pay apprentices a training wage in Year 2; the amount is agreed with each firm.',
	'placements_s3_p2' => 'The college does not set that figure and does not publish one. Year 1 never moves this work into a live home. The bench year stays on the rigs at 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield. The wage is a matter between the apprentice and the firm, agreed for that placement, and it is not part of the EUR 2,400 college fee.',
	'placements_s4_h' => 'What a firm commits to',
	'placements_s4_p1' => 'A firm that takes an apprentice commits to four days a week, one named engineer, and three visits from the college across the year. The engineer is the person under whom any gas or electrical work is done. The three visits are Grace Mwangi\'s, one each term, between the September start and the final assessment in June. Employers who want to talk about a place among the 18 can write to hello@kikan-college.example or call +00 44 555 0193 during office hours, Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30.',
	'placements_s4_p2' => 'Taking an apprentice is a training arrangement for the September to July year. It is not an agreement that the firm will hire when the year ends. Many firms do keep their apprentice on; we never promise it.',
	'placements_s5_h' => 'Next steps',
	'placements_s5_p1' => 'Apprentices in Year 1 meet the shape of Year 2 long before September: four days out, Friday here, one visit a term, 18 firms within 40 km. People who already run a firm and want to take an apprentice should contact the office in good time before applications for the next intake close on 30 April. Prospective apprentices who are still deciding can see the kind of work on a Tuesday visit at 16:00, or on a taster Saturday.',
	'placements_s5_p2' => 'The placement page is not a job board. If you are applying for yourself, the path is still the bench year first, at EUR 4,800, then the placement year at EUR 2,400. A EUR 300 deposit holds a Year 1 place and counts towards that first fee.',
	'placements_strip' => 'PLACEMENTS',
	'privacy_h' => 'Privacy',
	'privacy_lede' => 'Kikan College keeps the details you send us so we can answer an application, a Saturday booking, a message, or a request for the college letter. We do not sell those details.',
	'privacy_s1_h' => 'Who we are',
	'privacy_s1_p1' => 'Kikan College is the plumbing and heating apprenticeship college at 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield. The office email is hello@kikan-college.example and the phone is +00 44 555 0193. The office is open Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30. When this page says "we", it means the college. Rosa Lindqvist is principal. Questions about the details we hold can go to the same office address. We reply within five working days.',
	'privacy_s2_h' => 'What you send us',
	'privacy_s2_p1' => 'An application asks for your name, email, phone, confirmation that you are 18 or over, what you do now, why you want the trade, which September you want, whether you have been to a taster Saturday, and your consent that we may contact you about that application. A Saturday booking asks for your name, email, phone if you give it, the date, whether you bring a guest, access needs if you have them, and consent.',
	'privacy_s2_p2' => 'A contact message asks for your name, email, who you are, the message, and consent. The college letter asks for your email. We use those fields to answer you and to run the intake. We do not add other lists.',
	'privacy_s3_h' => 'How long we keep it',
	'privacy_s3_p1' => 'Application details are kept for the intake you named, and for the following intake if you ask us to hold them over. If you are offered a place, the details stay with the offer, the EUR 300 deposit, and the year fees. If you ask us to delete an application before an offer, we do that and confirm by email.',
	'privacy_s3_p2' => 'Saturday bookings are kept until that Saturday has passed, then deleted, unless you have also applied. Contact messages are kept long enough to reply and to refer back if you write again in the same year. College letter addresses are kept until you ask to be taken off. Tell us by email at hello@kikan-college.example.',
	'privacy_s4_h' => 'Who sees it',
	'privacy_s4_p1' => 'The office staff see applications, bookings, and messages. Instructors see what they need for a bench morning: your name and the September you named. Grace Mwangi sees placement details once you are in Year 2, shared with the firm you are placed with, limited to what that firm needs for the four days a week and the named engineer.',
	'privacy_s4_p2' => 'We do not pass your details to anyone else. We do not publish names from the forms. The three apprentice stories on this site are written with the people they name, and they are not drawn from the application form of a current applicant.',
	'privacy_s5_h' => 'Your consent and your requests',
	'privacy_s5_p1' => 'Each form asks you to agree that Kikan College may contact you about that application, booking, or message. The college letter is a request you send, and you are not on the list until we reply. You can ask what we hold, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it, by email to hello@kikan-college.example or by phone on +00 44 555 0193 during Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30.',
	'privacy_s5_p2' => 'We reply within five working days. Leaving the course before November is a fees matter, handled on the fees page, and it does not by itself delete the record of the year you attended. Ask if you want the record deleted as well.',
	'rosa_n' => 'Rosa Lindqvist',
	'rosa_p' => 'Rosa has been a master plumber for over thirty years and founded the college with Emeka in 2009. She leads Bench Hall A, where Year 1 learns pipework, soldering and drainage, and she still takes the first bench morning of every intake herself. She is strict about tidy benches and generous about mistakes.',
	'rosa_r' => 'Principal and co-founder',
	'rosa_t' => 'Teaches: pipework, soldering, bending, drainage',
