	'training-day_h' => 'A training day',
	'training-day_lede' => 'A training day in Year 1 runs Monday to Thursday from 07:45 to 15:30 in the bench halls, 465 minutes in all. Friday is the theory day, from 08:30 to 15:30, through the 38 weeks from September to July.',
	'training-day_rail' => 'A TRAINING DAY · 07:45',
	'training-day_s1_h' => 'Tool check and bench block one',
	'training-day_s1_p1' => 'The day opens at 07:45 with tool check and a toolbox talk, 15 minutes, until 08:00. At 08:00 the first bench block starts and runs to 10:15, 135 minutes of cutting, bending, and jointing. Morning work is based in the halls: pipework, soldering, and bending, with drainage in the same stretch of the week. People stand at their own bay under the task lamp. The rest of the hall stays dim.',
	'training-day_s1_p2' => 'This is the block where a new group learns the weight of a cutter and the set of a hand bender. Nobody is good at soldering in week one. By June you will not remember why it was hard. Hana Petrović says that to new groups in Bench Hall A, and the first month is built to make the sentence true.',
	'training-day_s2_h' => 'Break and the week\'s piece',
	'training-day_s2_p1' => 'Break is 10:15–10:35, 20 minutes. At 10:35 the second bench block starts and runs to 12:30, 115 minutes on the piece set for that week. The week\'s piece is where the morning\'s separate moves have to sit in one length of pipe: a cut that meets a bend, a bend that meets a joint, a joint that will face the rig after lunch. The time is long enough to redo a joint that is not ready, and short enough that the bay has to be left in order for lunch.',
	'training-day_s2_p2' => 'Instructors in Bench Hall A stay with soldering and pipework through this block. The piece is practice on a college bench, not work in a live home. Year 1 does not put gas work into occupied houses.',
	'training-day_s3_h' => 'Lunch and the boiler rig',
	'training-day_s3_p1' => 'Lunch is 12:30–13:15, 45 minutes. The rig block then runs 13:15–15:00, 105 minutes, in Bench Hall B. The work is a pressure test and fault-finding on the boiler rig. Two apprentices can share a rig, one watching an analogue gauge and one walking the pipe, with an instructor close by. The question of the block is whether the morning\'s joint holds, and where it does not.',
	'training-day_s3_p2' => 'Emeka Obi leads this hall and this rig. The rig is a practice rig under a task lamp, not a boiler in someone\'s kitchen. Fault-finding here means finding the weep and saying so. It does not mean gas work on a live home, which Year 1 does not include.',
	'training-day_s4_h' => 'Logbook, sign-off, bay swept',
	'training-day_s4_p1' => 'From 15:00 to 15:30, 30 minutes, the logbook is written, the day is signed off, and the bay is swept. That closes the Monday-to-Thursday day. Added up, tool check, two bench blocks, break, lunch, the rig, and the logbook run from 07:45 to 15:30, 465 minutes. The logbook entry is part of the bench assessments and the signed logbook, the record charged at EUR 220 per year.',
	'training-day_s4_p2' => 'We do not put another qualification\'s name on it. What matters at 15:30 is that the page matches the piece and the test you actually did, and that the bay is clear for the next morning\'s tool check. Hall hours on these four days are 07:45–15:30.',
	'training-day_s5_h' => 'Friday theory day',
	'training-day_s5_p1' => 'Friday starts later. Theory runs 08:30–12:30 in the theory room, 240 minutes, with Luis Carvalho. The subjects are water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings, and safe working. Lunch is 12:30–13:15, 45 minutes. From 13:15 to 15:30 the bench is open for practice and resits, 135 minutes. Hall hours on Friday are 08:30–15:30. This is the afternoon when someone who is behind on a joint can stay with it.',
	'training-day_s5_p2' => 'Hana Petrović has kept apprentices back on these Fridays for a first term of slow soldering. The college day in Year 2 is a Friday as well, while the other four days are spent with the placement firm. The theory room does not replace the bench; it sits beside it once a week.',
	'training-day_s6_h' => 'What you have with you',
	'training-day_s6_p1' => 'In week 1 of Year 1 the college issues the starter tool kit: a cutter, a bender, grips, a torch, and a case. It is yours to keep, and it is EUR 640. The same week you receive the workwear and safety pack: two overalls, boots, gloves, and glasses, at EUR 180. Those are the tools and the clothes of a bench day after week 1.',
	'training-day_s6_p2' => 'Safety glasses are worn for cutting and soldering. On a taster Saturday, boots and glasses are provided, and lunch is included. The evening refresher, for people already in the trade, is a separate Tuesday block from 18:00 to 21:00, six evenings at EUR 390, and is not part of the apprenticeship day. The office can confirm issue of the kit before your first Monday.',
	'training-day_s7_h' => 'Next steps',
	'training-day_s7_p1' => 'If you want to see the day before you apply, come on a taster Saturday, the first Saturday of the month, 09:00–15:00, not in August. A shorter look is the Tuesday visit at 16:00. Office hours for questions are Monday to Friday, 08:00–16:30, on +00 44 555 0193 or hello@kikan-college.example. Applications for a September start close on 30 April.',
	'training-day_s7_p2' => 'The address is 22 Foundry Lane, Wrenfield, and both halls are step-free on the ground floor. The bench morning after you apply is 90 minutes, on a single piece of pipe, and nobody expects it to be good. A EUR 300 deposit, after an offer, holds the place and counts towards Year 1.',
	'training-day_strip' => '07:45 TO 15:30',
	'util_here' => 'Getting here',
	'util_office' => 'Office Mon–Fri 08:00–16:30',
	'wd1_l' => 'Monday to Thursday, Bench Hall A',
	'wd1_v' => 'Rosa Lindqvist with Hana Petrović',
	'wd2_l' => 'Monday to Thursday, Bench Hall B and the boiler rig',
	'wd2_v' => 'Emeka Obi with Luis Carvalho',
	'wd3_l' => 'Friday, theory room',
	'wd3_v' => 'Luis Carvalho',
	'wd4_l' => 'Year 2, on site once a term',
	'wd4_v' => 'Grace Mwangi',
	'who_h' => 'Who the course is for',
	'who_li1' => 'No experience needed',
	'who_li2' => 'No upper age limit',
	'who_li3' => 'Minimum age 18',
	'who_n' => '01',
	'who_p1' => 'Most of our apprentices arrive from somewhere else. Some have run a café, driven a van or stacked shelves in a warehouse, and have decided that they would rather finish a day having made something that works. Nobody on the course is expected to know a compression fitting from a union. We start with the tape measure, the pipe cutter and the habit of checking every joint twice, and we teach the rest at the bench, one week at a time.',
	'who_p2' => 'Others are coming back to work after years of raising a family or caring for a relative. They tell us the bench year suits them because it is predictable: four set days, one theory day, and a workshop quiet enough to think in. There is no upper age limit, and the oldest person in a recent group was forty-six. What matters is that you turn up at a quarter to eight and are willing to be bad at soldering for a few weeks.',
	'who_p3' => 'A smaller group are school leavers over eighteen who want a bench rather than a lecture hall. They learn beside people twice their age and, in our experience, are better for it. You do not need a driving licence to apply, although many placement firms will ask about one in the second year. We would rather talk it through at a taster Saturday than read it on a form.',
	'who_sub' => 'Adults who want a trade they can see working.',
	'wordmark' => 'Kikan College',
	'y1_h' => 'Year 1 — the bench year',
	'y1_m1' => 'Sep: start',
	'y1_m2' => 'Feb: mid-year review',
	'y1_m3' => 'Jul: bench assessment',
	'y1_p' => 'Thirty-eight teaching weeks from September to July. Four days a week at the bench in Bench Hall A and Bench Hall B, and one day of theory: water regulations, heat loss, reading drawings and safe working. By the summer you have made, tested and signed off a full set of pipework, a boiler rig repair and a heat-pump connection.',
	'y2_h' => 'Year 2 — the placement year',
	'y2_m1' => 'Sep: placement starts',
	'y2_m2' => 'Each term: a site visit',
	'y2_m3' => 'Jun: final assessment',
	'y2_p' => 'Four days a week with one of our partner firms and one day back at college on Friday. You work beside a named engineer on real jobs, and our placement coordinator visits you on site once each term. A placement is a training year, not a job offer, although many firms do keep their apprentice on.',
	'years_h' => 'The two years',
	'years_n' => '03',
	'years_sub' => 'One year at the bench, one year placed with a working firm.',
	'endonym' => 'English',
);
